<title>UK: IBCA rates Helaba unit notes due 2000 AAA.</title>
<headline>IBCA rates Helaba unit notes due 2000 AAA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBCA, the European credit rating agency, said on Tuesday it had assigned a long-term rating of AAA to Helaba International Finance Plc, Dublin's $200 million 6.125 percent notes due 2000.</p>
<p>The issue is guaranteed by Landesbank Hessen-Thuringen Girozentrale.</p>
<p>&quot;The rating is based on the implied federal German guarantee for the obligations of the Landesbank,&quot; IBCA said in a statement.</p>
<p>--International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 4041</p>
</text>
